<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<Report xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/sqlserver/reporting/2016/01/reportdefinition" xmlns:rd="http://schemas.microsoft.com/SQLServer/reporting/reportdesigner">
  <!--
 EA CHECK (STUB/CHECK/STUB) CUSTOM RDLC

 PURPOSE
 =======
 This layout works with report extension 50195 "EA Check Vendor No.".

 It supports:
   * Up to 100 RefNbr-to-invoice mappings.
   * One Check per Vendor per Document No. selected or unselected.
   * Standard Business Central overflow/continuation check pages.
   * Split dataset rows where document information and paid amount are emitted
     on separate underlying records.
   * Matching RefNbr to the printed invoice number rather than assuming that
     array index equals the visible row number.

 IMPORTANT
 =========
 The standard check report only exposes 10 physical Stub2 rows per page.
 The 100 custom mappings are lookup values, not 100 visible rows on one page.
 Each printed page still displays at most the standard 10 check-detail rows.

 MAPPING CONTRACT WITH AL
 ========================
 EAFooterAppliesToDocNo1-100      = RefNbr / Vendor Ledger Document No.
 EAFooterExternalDocumentNo1-100 = Invoice Nbr / External Document No.
 EAFooterDueDate1-100             = Invoice Posting Date.

 The three groups are parallel arrays: index N in each group describes the
 same invoice application.
--><AutoRefresh>0</AutoRefresh>
  <DataSources>
    <DataSource Name="DataSource">
      <ConnectionProperties>
        <DataProvider>SQL</DataProvider>
        <ConnectString/>
      </ConnectionProperties>
      <rd:DataSourceID>a9d36e80-4c12-404c-9f4c-5e0f505e56a5</rd:DataSourceID>
    </DataSource>
  </DataSources>
  <!--
 DATASET DOCUMENTATION
 =====================
 The dataset below contains the standard Microsoft check-report fields plus
 custom EA fields supplied by report extension 50195.

 Custom fields 1-100 must remain synchronized with the AL extension. If the AL
 extension changes a field name, the matching RDLC Field/DataField pair must
 be updated here as well.
--><DataSets>
    <DataSet Name="DataSet_Result">
      <Query>
        <DataSourceName>DataSource</DataSourceName>
        <CommandText/>
      </Query>
      <Fields>
        <Field Name="GenJnlLine_Journal_Template_Name">
